\title{The UTF-8 sequences of a set of characters come as a list}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-17}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{stdlib}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{1085}
\import{base-macros}

\p{\code{\verb~|std::regex::alphabet::utf8::sequences(set)~} is new: the sequences of the encodings of the members of a \code{\verb~|CharSet~}, in the order of the bytes, as a list. \code{\verb~|fold_sequences~} is now a fold over that list and no longer calls its step from inside the recursion that cuts a stretch. Lowering a set of characters to bytes runs about a seventh fewer instructions. See [the session](ses-A1OD).}

\p{In review as \pr{1085}.}
